WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.503
Can an AI purchasing agent still deliver when stock disappears? Let's run that

00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:07.477
experiment in Rehearsal.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.618
The goal is three tents and six lights, within five hundred synthetic credits. Four

00:00:15.618 --> 00:00:21.632
methods range from fixed rules to practice and peer review. I'll choose peer

00:00:21.632 --> 00:00:25.208
review, select stock disappears, and start.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.050
First, the agent practices in an isolated world. An independent reviewer checks its

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.064
policy without purchasing tools. The live purchase clock has not started yet.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.999
Now the live world starts. Supplier A loses its tents. Nova chooses supplier B and

00:00:52.999 --> 00:00:58.723
authorizes three hundred and eighty credits. Watch the received count: payment

00:00:58.723 --> 00:01:05.155
alone is not delivery. The seller advances independently, and the verifier waits

00:01:05.155 --> 00:01:07.013
for the transaction evidence.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:20.884
All nine items arrived. The independent audit confirms the goal, with three hundred

00:01:20.884 --> 00:01:26.631
and eighty credits spent and nothing reserved. Practice, review, and purchasing

00:01:26.631 --> 00:01:31.461
used twenty-three model calls, costing about two point three cents.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:38.635
The timeline separates authorization, capture, and delivery. The review kept the

00:01:38.635 --> 00:01:44.718
existing policy in this run. A successful demonstration does not prove that peer

00:01:44.718 --> 00:01:46.970
review improves results.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:53.900
Refreshing retrieves the same experiment and its verified result. The runtime

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:59.160
session has been stopped, while the transaction evidence remains available.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:06.439
Nova runs through Strands on AgentCore. Lambda and DynamoDB own the commerce

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:12.790
records. Step Functions runs the seller and final audit, and S3 preserves the

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.274
evidence after the session stops.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:22.003
Try the live demo. Choose a condition, watch the purchase, and inspect what

00:02:22.003 --> 00:02:28.992
actually arrived. Source, evidence, and the editable AWS architecture are included.
